150.m:
Having performed a most sinful deed, I have reached a terrible rebirth;
and having been cooked in the hells, I have again reached the intermediate state.
Whatever persons commit evil deeds, such is their destination!”

Ever since, this has been well known as destroying piśāca-hood and great disease;
and men's great sins quickly go to destruction
by the mere remembrance of it.

152.m:
O best of rivers, you will be accompanied by all tīrthas;
whatever tīrthas there are in heaven, earth, and the underworld,
they will go to bathe in you, O Mother, when I am in Leo.'

With Śiva seated here, Nandin constantly [wanders] on the bank of the Gaṅgā;
he is dharma itself walking; therefore it is remembered as Nandītaṭa.
It is also the Ānanda tīrtha, because it increases all joy.'

165.m:
Brahmā said:
Thus asked, Dharmarāja related everything truly;
he made known without remainder the course of all those deeds.

Harṣaṇa said:
“My father is Tvaṣṭṛ’s son, terrifying, and my mother is Viṣṭi, terrifying;
and my brothers are high-spirited. By what means may they become peaceful in mind,

Brahmā said:
Having heard Dharma's words, Harṣaṇa went to the Gautamī;
being pure, he praised Hari, the lord of gods, and Hari was pleased.

166.m:
Brahmā said:
Patatritīrtha is declared as destroying disease and destroying sin;
by merely hearing of it, a man becomes one who has accomplished his purpose.

